# Desenvolvedor Backend Kotlin - Sênior

Published on SEPTEMBER 25, 2026

Applications open until NOVEMBER 24, 2026

---

Full-time employee

Remote

Also for PwD

---

## Job description

A FCamara está em busca de uma Pessoa Desenvolvedora Kotlin Sênior, para atuar em parceria com o melhor banco digital do Brasil, eleito por voto popular na 4o edição do prêmio CanalTech. Empresa que oferece um banco digital completo com produtos como, conta gratuita, cartão de crédito personalizado e investimento de renda fixa e variável.

## Responsibilities and assignments

• Preocupar-se com o produto desenvolvido, em todo seu ciclo de vida (desde a concepção da funcionalidade até a manutenção dela);

• Disponibilização de serviços vinculados ao produto;

• Solucionar problemas técnicos (bugs/incidentes/análises);

• Seguir políticas e processos definidos pelo cliente;

• Codificar testes unitários, funcionais, performance, seguindo diretrizes do time;

• Resolver problemas em produção em incidentes que impactam os clientes;

• Instrumentar as aplicações para extração de informações de performance, logs de funcionamento e métricas.

## Requirements and qualifications

**Hard Skill:**



• Linguagem Kotlin;

• Framework Spring;

• Boas práticas de desenvolvimento de software – TDD, DDD e Clean Code;

• Práticas/Frameworks ágeis: SCRUM e KANBAN;

• Instanciamento virtual de servidores AWS (SQS, S3);

• Banco de Dados MongoDB, Postgres e Redis;

• Aplicação de testes unitários;

• Gerenciador de código GIT Flow.

• Arquitetura orientada a eventos




**Soft Skill:**



• Capacidade de comunicação clara e objetiva;

• Espírito de equipe e capacidade de resolução de conflitos;

• Habilidade de trabalhar em equipes ágeis e multidisciplinares;

• Criatividade e proatividade para imaginar diferentes cenários de uso das aplicações.




**Seria legal se você tivesse:**



• Experiência na plataforma de conteinerização Docker;

• Experiência com Javascript;

• Experiência na Plataforma Apigee

## Process stages

1. 1Registration
2. 2Triagem
3. 3Entrevista R&S
4. 4Entrevista Técnica
5. 5CV enviado ao cliente
6. 6Entrevista Cliente
7. 7Carta Proposta
8. 8Hiring

## Transformamos mundos sonhados em trajetórias reais.🧡🚀

**Aqui somos #SangueLaranja!**



Estamos há 17 anos no mercado, lado a lado com nossos clientes, proporcionando experiências transformadoras.

Somos um ecossistema de tecnologia e inovação, com expansão global; Além do Brasil estamos presentes na Europa e Reino Unido com escritórios em Portugal, Londres, Dubai e Holanda. 🌎

**F de Formação: acreditamos na prática da cultura do compartilhamento, no senso de comunidade, e que o conhecimento**

**tem o poder da transformação!**

Possuímos iniciativas, e ações sociais, que promovem o desenvolvimento, como a comunidade tech Orange Juice, o Programa de Formação,

nossa escola de liderança e diversas parcerias com ONGs e Edtechs.

**Na FCamara todos são bem-vindos, para nós, Diversidade, Respeito e Ética, são elementos inegociáveis e fazem parte do nosso DNA.**

**E aí, está pronto para fazer parte de um time incrível e ser protagonista da própria história?**

**Role summary/purpose of job**

 As part of a team working routinely across the weekend (Friday to Monday -

Some flexibility may be considered ), the Weekend LSS will provide fee-earning legal services support to the global firm.

The work will range from urgent, short-term tasks requiring immediate support, to longer term projects and tasks where the LSS will act as an integrated member of Practice Group teams alongside associates from across the global firm.

**Key responsibilities and deliverables**

The Weekend LSS will contribute to an inclusive working environment where all colleagues are treated with fairness and respect, applying the ‘Being Freshfields’ principles at all times.

The Weekend LSS will contribute to the Hub’s culture of quality, striving for excellence in standard of output and being a positive role model within the team.

The Weekend LSS will work as part of a team carrying out a range of tasks to support our global client needs. The Weekend LSS will have the opportunity to engage with fee earners from all fields, but will have specific focus on Global M&A and Capital, Dispute Resolution and Anti-Trust Competition and Trade practice groups.

With experience, there are opportunities to specialize in areas such as Capital Markets, International Arbitration and Financial Regulatory.

Core operational tasks to support client mandates include, but are not limited to:

* Due Diligence reviews;
* Document review for an investigation or at the disclosure stage of a litigation;
* Document cross-checking, making document amendments;
* Proofreading of documents including contracts, agreements and transcripts;
* Reviewing and marking up non-disclosure agreements;
* Document collation, version control and document review;
* Data Room management;
* Database entry/coding, database searching and database maintenance;
* Hard copy document management;
* Legal research (manual or electronic); and
* Creating and populating tables, schedules and agendas
* Bundle preparation (e.g. witness bundles and trial bundles) includes document searches to identify which documents are to be included in a bundle, bulk printing, arranging photocopying, copy-checking, indexing, file preparation and collation. If documents are stored electronically, it may also include database tagging and/or searching;

This work will be carried out following established processes and using workflow and work allocation systems as required.

The Weekend LSS will also contribute to the development and continuous improvement of the CDG by assisting with requirements gathering, process mapping, process evaluation and support documentation as required.

The Weekend LSS will maintain a daily log of all activity and a record of time spent.  They will establish and maintain effective working relationships with all levels of Freshfields employees.  They will identify and escalate issues in a timely and effective manner.

The Weekend LSS will be expected to be proactive in the acquisition of skills using Artificial Intelligence (AI) and in the use of AI wherever reasonable and approved in their work.

The Weekend LSS will have a four-day working week with standard hours as follows:

Friday         9am – 6pm

Saturday    9am – 6pm

Sunday       9am – 6pm

Monday      9am – 6pm

The Weekend LSS will be required to be present in the Manchester office for at least two days each week and as required by the firm.

The Weekend LSS will prioritize ad hoc tasks received towards the end of the traditional working week and over the UK weekend, providing support for global offices in different time zones.  This will allow the Hub to respond to growing demand for out-of-hours working and short-notice requests.

The overlap with LSS teams on Friday and Monday will also mean the opportunity to work on other long-term projects as part of a larger collaborative effort and allow for effective handover between teams.

Other tasks that are legal and reasonable as required.

**Key requirements**

**Professional qualifications**

* Candidates must hold an undergraduate degree, preferably in law, or equivalent.

**It is preferred that:**

* candidates holding an undergraduate degree in an area other than law will have completed a recognized law conversion course; and/or
* candidates will have completed the LPC or BPTC or be overseas qualified or equivalent (preferred LPC electives for the role include: Acquisitions, Banking and Capital Markets, Commercial Law, Corporate Finance, Intellectual Property Competition; and Commercial Disputes Resolution).

**Experience**

* Previous corporate paralegal experience in a large law firm would be an advantage but is not essential.

**Technical requirements**

**Essential:**

* Strong computer skills and experience in using MS Office tools (in particular Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams and SharePoint).
* Excellent attention to detail;
* The ability to work in accordance with established processes;
* The ability to complete work to tight deadlines when required; and
* The ability to work with large amounts of information.

**Preferred:**

* Experience of using document management systems;
* Knowledge of legal search engines such as Butterworths, LexisNexis, OJ online and Justis;
* Experience of using a range of legal technologies, including different data room providers, artificial intelligence and document review platforms; and
* Fluency in a second language with an ability to translate legal documents into English: key languages of interest are: Arabic; Cantonese; Mandarin; French; German; Italian; Spanish.

**Competencies**

* Excellent attention to detail;
* The ability to work in accordance with established processes;
* The ability to complete work to tight deadlines when required; and
* The ability to work with large amounts of information.
* Excellent oral and written communication skills with the ability to listen, clarify and share information easily;
* The ability to build strong working relationships;
* The ability to identify and communicate opportunities to improve the way that work is done;
* A diplomatic and adaptable team working style;
* Strong commercial awareness;
* Dedication to meeting and exceeding customer expectations;
* Resilient and able to remain calm and positive under pressure and when dealing with ambiguity;
* Actively manage personal learning and development; and
* A commitment to the highest levels of integrity.

**Inclusion**

Freshfields is an equal opportunities employer and all applications received by the firm will be considered on the basis of their merit alone. We welcome applications from all suitably qualified individuals regardless of background. All offers of employment will be conditional on the candidate having/securing the right to work in the UK in the role in question and providing the firm with evidence of that right (as required by the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006) prior to employment commencing.

Freshfields is a Ban the Box employer. We ask applicants to disclose criminal convictions only if and when a conditional job offer is made. A conviction does not automatically lead to withdrawal of the offer: we make decisions on a case-by-case basis and take a number of relevant factors into account (e.g. the role you are applying for and the circumstances of the offence). You would have the opportunity to discuss the matter with us before we make a decision.

**COMO SEU TRABALHO PODE TRANSFORMAR O MUNDO!**   

***Missão da área:***

A área de Performance e Controle é o motor de inteligência avançada, engenharia de métricas e governança de dados da nossa operação de Customer Experience (CX).

Nossa missão é transformar grandes volumes e diferentes fontes de dados em insights estratégicos, automações e soluções escaláveis que maximizem a eficiência operacional e a experiência do cliente.

Atuamos na vanguarda analítica do negócio, combinando dados quantitativos e qualitativos, modelagens em Power BI, extrações via SQL e soluções com Inteligência Artificial para identificar causas-raiz, antecipar tendências e apoiar a tomada de decisão das lideranças com uma governança de dados robusta.

***Aqui suas responsabilidades serão:***

* Investigar problemas e oportunidades relacionados à experiência do cliente e à eficiência operacional, utilizando dados quantitativos e qualitativos para identificar causas e direcionar ações;
* Analisar indicadores de CX, como CSAT, performance, SLA e produtividade, identificando tendências, desvios e oportunidades de melhoria;
* Transformar análises em recomendações práticas, conectando dados, operação, processos e experiência do cliente;
* Estruturar e acompanhar projetos de melhoria contínua, desde a identificação do problema até a implementação e mensuração dos resultados;
* Atuar em parceria com lideranças, operação, processos, produto e tecnologia na construção de soluções e na evolução das iniciativas;
* Desenvolver e acompanhar indicadores, dashboards em Power BI e rotinas de governança que apoiem a tomada de decisão;
* Utilizar automações e ferramentas de dados para tornar processos de acompanhamento, análise e comunicação mais eficientes e escaláveis;
* Explorar e construir agentes utilizando Inteligência Artificial para solucionar problemas de CX, avaliando oportunidades, testando abordagens e mensurando resultados;
* Cruzar diferentes fontes de informação, como indicadores, comentários de clientes e dados operacionais, para construir uma visão mais completa dos problemas e oportunidades;
* Comunicar análises, insights e recomendações de forma clara para diferentes públicos, adaptando a profundidade técnica ao interlocutor;
* Ter autonomia para identificar problemas ainda não estruturados, conduzir investigações e propor soluções;
* Considerar o impacto das decisões na experiência do cliente, na operação e nos resultados do negócio.

***Qualificações que você precisa ter:***

* Ensino superior completo em Economia, Engenharias, Estatística, Ciência de Dados, Gestão ou áreas correlatas;
* Conhecimento avançado em Power BI para construção e governança de dashboards;
* Conhecimento em SQL para extração e análise de dados;
* Conhecimento avançado em Excel/Google Sheets;
* Experiência com ferramentas de automação;
* Experiência com análise de indicadores de Customer Experience;
* Conhecimento em metodologias de qualidade e melhoria contínua;
* Experiência com ferramentas e aplicações de Inteligência Artificial.

***Habilidades que são diferenciais:***

* Capacidade analítica avançada: facilidade para trabalhar com números, indicadores e diferentes fontes de informação, buscando entender não apenas o que está acontecendo, mas por que está acontecendo;
* Visão de negócio e cliente: capacidade de conectar indicadores de CX aos impactos para clientes, operação e negócio;
* Resolução de problemas: perfil investigativo, curioso e pragmático, capaz de transformar problemas pouco estruturados em planos de ação;
* Orientação para dados: capacidade de utilizar dados para embasar decisões, sem perder a visão crítica de que nem todas as respostas estarão nos indicadores.

**POR QUE TRANSFORMAR AO NOSSO LADO?**

* Plano de saúde e odontológico com cobertura nacional, sem custo para o colaborador e com coparticipação para cônjuge e dependentes;
* Vale refeição/alimentação (Flash - bandeira Visa);
* Benefício flexível (Flash Multibenefícios - bandeira Visa), podendo ser destinado à alimentação, refeição, mobilidade (aplicativos de transporte, combustível, transporte público em SP), cultura, saúde e educação;
* Previdência privada;
* Vale transporte;
* Seguro de vida;
* Wellhub;
* Auxílio creche para filhos de até cinco anos;
* Budget de educação: valor destinado aos investimentos relacionados à sua educação, de forma a contribuir para desenvolver e potencializar suas competências;
* Incentivo ao aprendizado de idiomas por meio de plataforma online;
* Baby On Board: benefício oferecido para as pessoas que estão se preparando para a maternidade e paternidade;
* Licença maternidade estendida (180 dias);
* Licença Paternidade estendida (30 dias);
* Conexa Saúde: acesso online gratuito a profissionais da área da saúde - Nutricionista e Psicólogo;
* Participação anual nos lucros e resultados da companhia (PLR);
* Hotmart Recharge: bônus de 30% do salário bruto mensal, pago após cumprir o período aquisitivo de férias de 30 dias.

# Cost Controller

* Hybrid
* + London, Greater London, United Kingdom•

  +1 more
* Finance

## Job description

**Join us as we work to unlock the value of offshore wind!** JERA Nex bp is a new joint venture between JERA, Japan’s largest power generation company, and bp, one of the world’s leading energy companies. Established to unlock the potential of offshore wind across the globe, our talented team, exciting pipeline and solid capital commitment give us the potential to become one of the world’s most successful offshore wind companies.

We entered the market with a portfolio of operational and development assets, alongside the resources, capabilities and resilience to deliver offshore wind energy at scale.

**Why this role matters:**

Offshore wind is a complex, uncertain and expensive industry. From bidding, through construction, installation and operation, costs are in the $billions over multiple years and require many strategic partnerships across a dynamic geopolitical and environmental landscape. There are complex financial structures in place that need to be carefully managed with both cash and financial reporting implications across multiple entities. The Corporate Controlling team are essential for ensuring these positions are clearly understood, optimised and carefully managed.  

**In this role you will**:

Work in very close cooperation with the Commercial director;

* Provide finance oversight for complex and large capex projects in development or construction phase;
* Be accountable for the development and implementation of an effective and efficient project cost management system;
* Lead the entire budgeting, forecasting & reporting process over the development & construction lifetime of different projects and monitor the actual spendings;
* Be responsible for providing project leaders with high quality cost related insights to facilitate decision making processes including variance analysis and Trends;
* Provide regular and reliable assessments of the VOWD (Value of Work Done) ensuring that accruals stand up to audit;
* Provide ongoing commitment and expenditure tracking and control, ensuring compliance with project WBS and budgets;
* Monitor and control staffing requirements of the project;
* Responsible for the preparation of monthly financial reports and presentations towards different stakeholders (management team, board of directors, banks, shareholders, internal departments);
* Have a good understanding of the development & construction process of a large capex project (financial, technical, contractual, interfaces, risks);
* Responsible for the analytical masterdata of the project(s) reporting in SAP;
* Participate and contribute to continuously improving reporting, controlling and planning processes;
* Work with Accounting to achieve an accurate financial close each period for Corporate entities;

## Job requirements

**To be successful in the role you will bring**:

* You obtained a Bachelor/Master degree in finance or related disciple;

* You have at least 7 years’ experience and 3 years’ experience in a similar role. Experience from the on- & offshore wind sector or the oil & gas sector is a plus.
* You have a good ability to understand the complex financial & technical business and its interactions;
* You have in-depth knowledge of analytical and accounting concepts, and you are familiar with SAP and reporting systems;
* You are an advanced user of MS Office and you have an interest in financial modelling;
* You are organized enough to be able to track multiple projects and perform several tasks at the same time;
* You are accurate and have strong analytical skills;
* You have strong social and communicative skills and can work both in team as autonomous;

**What you can expect from us:**

**Working at JERA Nex bp means being part of a global leader in offshore wind, where innovation, collaboration, and sustainability drive everything we do. You’ll enjoy:**

* A collaborative and inclusive work culture, with space for team-building and social activities

* Flexible working hours and the opportunity to work from home, with regular in-person connection

* Opportunities for career growth and professional development in a fast-growing international company.

**As we build our company, we are driven by:**

**Care for each other and our world –** we leave egos at the door, are inclusive, collaborative and open to new ideas

**A spirit of ingenuity -** we are pioneers and innovators making the impossible possible

**A commitment to unlocking value from offshore wind –** we aim to make offshore wind sustainable, affordable and accessible to the countries & communities we serve.

**About JERA Nex bp**

JERA Nex bp is a purpose-built offshore wind company committed to unlocking the power of offshore wind by developing high-quality, competitive projects.

A 50:50 joint venture between JERA Co. and bp, JERA Nex bp is an end-to-end developer, owner and operator with more than fifteen years of experience in operating offshore wind projects.

Headquartered in London, with offices across Europe, Asia, and Australia, JERA Nex bp has a portfolio of operational and development projects across nine countries, and draws on a rich heritage of pioneering offshore wind in Asia Pacific and the North Sea.

# Data Protection Consultant

## Join WorkNest on a 9-month FTC as a Data Protection Consultant, supporting clients with DSARs, GDPR compliance and privacy projects while developing your expertise.

Reporting to our Data Protection Team Lead, the Data Protection Consultant will work directly with our clients to scope, analyse and implement GDPR practices, processes and procedures. In addition to this, the GDPR Consultant role will complete and oversee the delivery of gap analyses, implementations and DPO services to our wide variety of customers.

In this role, you will be providing support with the handling and processing of Data Subject Access Requests (DSARs). The role will involve assisting with reviewing information, carrying out redactions where required, and supporting the wider team throughout the DSAR process. Full training and guidance will be provided, making this a great opportunity for someone looking to develop their knowledge and experience in data protection and compliance.

Due to the nature of the role, the position requires the ability to manage multiple clients simultaneously whilst ensuring a customer-centric approach.

**Responsibilities:**

* Lead and manage GDPR projects, ensuring delivery is in line with client expectations;

* Act as an SME for all GDPR, PECR and other privacy-related matters;

* Work closely with the Sales to scope projects;

* Conduct GDPR Gap Analyses and GDPR Implementations (data mapping, developing policies and procedures, records of processing, DPIAs, LIAs etc.);

* Work closely with the GDPR Team Lead to oversee the project management, scheduling and delivery of all GDPR projects, completing and updating relevant records for reporting purpose.

* Deliver GDPR training as well as supporting clients with GDPR documentation, data breaches, and data subject access requests;

* Write content for articles and blog posts on data protection related topics;

* Any other appropriate job duties in line with the associated skill and experience of the post holder.

**Skills and experience required:**

* Direct experience of leading Data Protection consultancy projects (scoping, gap analysis, and implementation) across small, medium and large businesses, with a strong understanding of tailored service delivery to suit client size and requirements;

* Qualified in one or more of the following: GDPR Practitioner (or equivalent), Certified DPO, IAPP CIPP/E qualification, Law Degree with a focus on GDPR/Privacy;

* Knowledge of CCPA and other international privacy laws highly desirable;

* Specific region or sector expertise (e.g., Scotland, Northern Ireland, health and social care, financial services) highly desirable

* Strong Microsoft Office skills;

**Personal Attributes:**

* Ability to remain calm under pressure and meet deadlines;

* Strong organisational skills with a high attention to detail;

* Ability to prioritise and handle multiple tasks at any given time;

* Pro-active and enthusiastic with a can do attitude;

* Excellent verbal and written communication skills;

* Strong commercial acumen;

* Ability to work on own initiative as well as being a team player;

* Willingness to learn.

**Other:**

* International and national travel should be expected as part of the role;

* Must be eligible to live and work in the UK;

**WorkNest Benefits:**

* **Annual leave:** 25 days, increasing by 1 day per each completed year of service up to a maximum of 28 days, plus statutory bank holidays which will be paid.
* **Birthday Day Off:** One additional day off for your birthday, to be taken a week either side of your birthday
* **Private Medical Insurance** Discounted individual coverage (available after successful completion of probation). Full individual cover after 3 years.
* **Subsidised Gym / Wellbeing membership** £15 per month subsidised membership (available after probation)
* **VITO Days:** 2 paid volunteer days per year (available after probation)
* **Health Cash Plan** Cash back on dental, optical and more, Employee Assistance Programme, Virtual GP and wellbeing resources (available from day one)
* **UK Electric Vehicle Salary Sacrifice Scheme** Subject to eligibility criteria
* **Enhanced Family Related Leave Pay** subject to qualifying periods **Company Sick Pay** 2 weeks enhanced sick pay (available after probation)
* **Pension** Standard Life Salary Sacrifice Pension - 3% Employer / 5% Employee. Auto-enrolment after 3 months, with the option to opt in or opt out
* **Sophos Home Premium** Cover for your family personal laptops
* **Employee referral scheme** £1000 paid to you for successful employee referrals
* **Social events**

If you’re looking for an opportunity to develop your career in data protection and work with a wide range of clients, we’d love to hear from you.

At WorkNest, you’ll be part of a supportive and collaborative team where you’ll have the opportunity to build your expertise, take on new challenges and make a real impact for our clients.

If this sounds like the right opportunity for you, we’d encourage you to apply and tell us why you’d be a great addition to the team.

# Regional Sales Manager - EMEA

Ipswich, GBR

* Recruiting Company: Textron Specialized Vehicles
* Job Level: Individual Contributor
* Job Field: Sales
* Reqid: 343645

**Regional Sales Manager - EMEA**

**Description**

**About Us**

Textron Specialized Vehicles are a global manufacturer of golf cars, utility and personal transportation vehicles, side-by-sides, all-terrain vehicles, professional turf-care equipment, and ground support equipment.

At Ransomes Jacobsen Ltd, we design and manufacture professional turf-care equipment under the brands of Ransomes and Jacobsen. Our mission is to be the premier supplier of high-quality and environmentally conscious turf equipment, providing superior performance for our customers. From prestigious championship golf courses to the World Cup, for more than a century, the most important turf in the world has been manicured by our brand.

We recognise that our success, and future success, is tied directly to our people. We are looking to welcome a Regional Sales Manager to join our journey in delivering perfectly groomed turf.

**About the role**

This is a full-time role based remotely, covering our EMEA region. While we welcome applications from across the UK, the ideal location for this role is the Midlands or North of England.

Your responsibilities include, but are not limited to:

* Achieving the monthly, quarterly and annual sales objectives set for your regional zone, as well as any targets that may be set from time to time, via a Hybrid sales approach;
* Executing & contributing to the dealer/distribution strategy of your zone to enable Ransomes Jacobsen to improve its sales;
* Achieving all margin objectives that are set, and controlling outstanding receivables for customers you are responsible for;
* Agreeing an Annual Business Plan with each dealer/distributor in your zone where appropriate, against specific objectives set by the Company. Additionally, to put in place Dealer/Distributor Development Plans that increase the professionalism and effectiveness of each dealer/distributor;
* Enhancing brand perception by carrying out end user visits, with or without dealer/distributor sales personnel present, and performing product demonstrations to build end-user relationships;
* Identifying, developing and promoting new sales opportunities via a Hybrid sales approach;
* Identifying and establishing an independent and financially secure dealer/distributor network for the Ransomes Jacobsen product range;
* Identifying dealer/distributor training needs and recommending/executing product and sales training as necessary;
* Keeping updated records on all dealers and customers, including: providing timely visit reports following all visits; a weekly itinerary; and, a detailed monthly report on all aspects of your sales operation;
* Identifying and reporting vulnerabilities in the Company’s sales activities;
* Safely maintaining and protecting all Company assets controlled by yourself;
* Ensuring all Company systems, policies and procedures are followed and implemented correctly;
* Promoting and assisting with the promotion of all Ransomes Jacobsen brands, regardless of whether the brand is within your remit.

**Qualifications**

**About You**

As a Regional Sales Manager, we would ask you bring the following skills and experience:

* Educated to Degree/A Level or equivalent;
* Minimum of five years’ commercial experience and three years’ experience in a related industry;
* IT literate;
* Full driving licence;
* Excellent commercial awareness and interpersonal skills;
* Customer service oriented;
* Strong decision-making and problem-solving skills;
* Ability to manage workload and excel at prioritising and organising tasks;
* Technical aptitude.

**Why us?**

* Work life balance promoted with every other Friday off;
* 30 days annual leave;
* Competitive rate of pay, reviewed annually;
* Enhanced Company pension;
* Life assurance of four times your annual salary;
* Comprehensive Employee Assistance Program for you and your immediate family;
* Access to Textron University’s self-service training platform;
* Eye care scheme;
* Discounts on gym memberships, shopping and travel through Perks at Work;
* Winter flu vaccination voucher.

**Design Engineer Graduate**

**Description**

**About Us**

Textron Specialized Vehicles are a global manufacturer of golf cars, utility and personal transportation vehicles, side-by-sides, all-terrain vehicles, professional turf-care equipment, and ground support equipment.

At Ransomes Jacobsen Ltd, we design and manufacture professional turf-care equipment under the brands of Ransomes and Jacobsen. Our mission is to be the premier supplier of high-quality and environmentally conscious turf equipment, providing superior performance for our customers. From prestigious championship golf courses to the World Cup, for more than a century, the most important turf in the world has been manicured by our brand.

**About the Role**

This is a full-time role based at our manufacturing facility in Ipswich, Suffolk.

As a Design Engineer I, you will support the delivery of high-quality mechanical design work across a range of projects. Working under the guidance of senior-engineering staff, you will contribute to the development of reliable, cost-effective, and manufacturable solutions that meet performance targets and regulatory requirements.

Your responsibilities include, but are not limited to:

* Produce mechanical designs that meet defined technical, performance, reliability, and cost requirements;
* Create and maintain accurate engineering documentation, including drawings, Bills of Materials (BOMs), assembly instructions, and supporting technical publications in line with the Engineering Change process;
* Apply best-practice design principles and utilise in-house standards, approved reference materials, and standard components wherever appropriate;
* Ensure all designs are practical, efficient, and cost-effective to manufacture by working closely with Manufacturing and Production teams;
* Ensure designs are developed in context, maintaining compatibility with adjacent components, assemblies, and wider system architectures;
* Perform component-level CAE/FEA analyses to support design decisions, verify performance, and identify opportunities for improvement;
* Integrate mistake-proofing, clear visual guidance, or simplified features into designs to reduce the potential for assembly errors or rework;
* Collaborate with other Engineers and internal departments when implementing new design concepts or engineering approaches;
* Interpret and incorporate relevant industry standards, directives, and regulatory requirements into product designs;
* Support the engineering team in ensuring all documentation and designs comply with applicable quality and safety expectations;
* Assist in the development of test plans and validation activities to ensure key design elements and performance objectives are met;
* Support testing activities as required, including preparing test articles, reviewing results, and contributing to design refinements.

**Qualifications**

**About You**

As a Design Engineer I, we would ask you bring the following skills and experience:

* Bachelor’s degree or equivalent in an Engineering discipline, ideally Mechanical Engineering.
* Experience designing with a range of materials, including steels, plastics and alloys.
* Exposure to engineering development processes such as prototyping, testing, or design-for-manufacture desirable.
* Knowledge of DFME and PFMEA.
* Proficiency in CAD software (NX preferred) required.
* Familiarity with FEA tools, ideally ANSYS, to support basic analysis and validation activities.
* Hands-on approach, with the ability to work effectively within a multidisciplinary team to take design concepts through to medium-volume production.
* Self-motivated, capable of working independently toward defined objectives with minimal supervision.
